# CCTV REVIEW SUMMARY — cam16_stream-16, VISAT T JUNCTION

**Source:** cam16_stream-16.mp4 — 720 minutes (minutes 0–719), Saturday 13-06-2026 into 14-06-2026.

## 1. SCENE

The camera overlooks Visat T Junction, a signalised T-junction with a zebra crossing, left kerb/footpath with bus shelter(s), a central island, and shops/kiosk area on the far side. Footage spans the full 24-hour cycle: the early period (minutes 0–~524) is night-time/dark, transitioning through infrared/greyscale (minutes ~500–519) to dusk colour, then overcast daylight from approximately minute 625 onward. Night segments show heavy glare, motion blur, amber signal phases and lens flare; roads appeared wet/damp with rain reflections at minutes 205, 209, 211, 213, 218, 269, 478, 491, 493, 501 (droplet bloom), 510, 527 and 545. Camera-facing signals showed red/amber for much of minutes 525–624, cycling red/amber/green in daylight hours.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE

Traffic was continuous for the full 720 minutes, dominated throughout by:

- **Motorcycles/scooters** — the most numerous vehicle class (roughly 6–25 per minute), riders mostly in white/light clothing, frequently two-up with pillions, many apparently helmetless (e.g. minutes 9, 14, 54, 261, 275, 709).
- **Yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws** — several per minute throughout, with occasional blue, grey, white, cream, black/green, green/teal and yellow variants (up to 8–10 in minute 63 and 6–8 in minute 94).
- **Cars** — predominantly white (hatchbacks, sedans, SUVs, MPVs), plus black, dark grey, silver/grey, red, maroon/dark-red, blue, orange and occasional yellow taxi-style vehicles.
- **Buses** — very frequent in all periods: white coaches, blue-and-white, blue-and-yellow, red/red-and-white, blue-and-orange, orange/red, green, cream and double-decker buses (red, yellow, blue-and-yellow, orange).
- **Goods vehicles** — tarpaulin-covered trucks, tippers, box trucks, tankers (white, brown/red, yellow/white), cement mixers, flatbeds and trailers, tractors with trailers, goods three-wheelers, three-wheeled carts (one animal-drawn cart, minute 169).
- **Vans/ambulances** — white vans/tempos throughout; ambulance-type vans with flashing blue/red lights at minutes 0, 2, 54, 59, 63, 106, 152, 155, 246, 292, 419, 469, 643, 688-689.
- **Others** — cyclists (minutes 2, 7, 10, 21, 23, 26, 458, 555, 571-572, 576-578, 586, 591, 598, 601, 605, 613, 623, 625, 644, 676-678, 680, 690), a white low-bed truck carrying a vehicle (minute 6), a backhoe loader (minutes 628, 667, 688-689), an olive-green military-style truck (minute 710), a car carrier (period 650–674), a white police-style SUV (minute 700) and a police-style patrol vehicle (minute 38).

**Pedestrians** were present throughout but sparse from ~minute 325 onward: heavier early (up to eight crossing/waiting in minute 16), mainly individuals and small groups using the zebra or waiting at kerbs. Notable figures include a man in a black t-shirt standing on the crossing for the whole of minute 70; a person sitting on the kerb with a dog (minute 29); a man in all white standing at the kerb for minutes 207–209 without crossing; a man in a pink shirt standing mid-carriageway for most of minute 572; and a man with a white shoulder bag lingering on the zebra through minutes 700–701. A person in khaki/traffic-police-style clothing was near the left kerb through much of minute 45.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED

### CONFIRMED
- **Maruti Suzuki Swift**, white hatchback, plate not legible, direction of travel not stated, minute 711.

(Other legible text — "SODHA" bus rear, minute 32; "BARMER" bus, minute 99; "JAY AMBE" bus, minute 110; "INTAS" bus rear, minute 221; "BURAQ LOGISTICS" box truck, minute 535; "M.R. TRAVELS" coach, minutes 141 and 583; "SABAR EXPRESS" coach, minute 585; "AMBICA" bus, minute 587; "SHREE"/"SHREE TRAVELS" coaches, minutes 2 and 716; "SHIVAM" coach, minute 664; "NIRMA" bus, minute 688; "BHAVANI" coach, minute 699 — are fleet/company names, not make/model identifications.)

### PROBABLE (unconfirmed)
- **Bajaj RE-class auto-rickshaw** (unconfirmed), yellow-green, minute 542.
- **AMC/GSRTC-style red city buses** (unconfirmed), minutes 536.
- **Ford EcoSport** — white compact SUV with rear-mounted spare wheel, consistent with this model (plate not legible), minute 659.

## 4. REGISTRATIONS READ

None legible. No registration plate was read at any point in the 720 minutes — all plates were illegible due to night lighting, glare, distance and motion blur. No automatic single reads were recorded to note.

## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS

- **Minute 0** — white ambulance/police-type van with active blue-red emergency lights through the junction (~34s, 44–49s).
- **Minute 6** — white low-bed truck carrying another vehicle.
- **Minutes 13, 15** — pick-up/truck carrying standing passengers in open rear (minute 15, ~45s).
- **Minutes 27, 68, 200, 370, 420–424, 685** — animals on or near the carriageway: pale animal possibly dog/cow in carriageway (minute 27, ~45s); dog near left kerb (minutes 68, 200, 370); stray dogs on left footpath (minutes 420–424); dog entering bottom-left (minute 685, ~50s).
- **Minutes 43, 160, 156** — unusual crossings: two-wheeler on the footpath side of the zebra (minute 43, 29–34s); black-and-yellow three-wheeler crossing diagonally over the zebra area (minute 160); scooter with two apparently helmetless riders stopped on the zebra from ~49s (minute 156).
- **Minutes 62, 64–65** — white car parked at bottom-left kerb with driver door open from ~25s (minute 62); motorcycle lying on its side at the left kerb with a person in white shirt standing beside it (minutes 64–65).
- **Minute 84** — queues building from ~45s.
- **Minutes 151–153** — blue-and-yellow tipper truck parked with beacon/work lights on.
- **Minute 169** — animal-drawn cart heavily loaded with goods crossing the junction.
- **Minute 190s** — white car braking/stopped near crossing (minute 195); dark SUV turning across the near end of the crossing (minute 198).
- **Minute 200** — white box truck turning right-to-left appeared to lose part of its load, spilling a large light-coloured sand/gravel-like substance across the carriageway from ~15s onward (the most significant incident in the footage).
- **Minutes 245, 290, 296** — stationary vehicles at the crossing: auto-rickshaw stopped at left edge with person standing beside it from ~45s (minute 245); auto-rickshaw stationary on left carriageway for the whole minute joined by a motorcycle and 2–3 pedestrians (minute 290); black-and-yellow auto stationary on the zebra/stop line (minute 296).
- **Minute 406–408** — motorcycle with rider carrying a box stopped at left stop line and stationary across three minutes.
- **Minutes 479** — motorcycle with two riders appearing low/tilted with a person beside it (~40s).
- **Minutes 525, 529, 545, 702, 709** — two-wheelers crossing on red/amber phases; free flow through the junction despite camera-facing red (minutes 702, 709).
- **Minute 517, 518–523, 510, 516, 629–632, 681, 688–689, 695–698** — parked/stationary vehicles: white car parked at left kerb from ~20s (minute 517); blue city bus stopped at left bus stop for the full duration of minutes 518–523; dark vehicles parked off-carriageway (minutes 510, 516); white tempo truck parked on verge (minutes 629–632); blue tarpaulin truck parked left throughout minute 681; auto-rickshaw parked at left kerb for entire minutes 695–698 with people standing beside it.
- **Minute 524** — white sedan carrying a concealed load.
- **Minute 540** — white SUV/ambulance-type vehicle braking across the zebra.
- **Minutes 543** — flock of pigeons settling on the carriageway.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION

- **Minute 16** — at least eight pedestrians crossing/waiting at the junction (largest stated group).
- **Minute 41** — group of 4–8 pedestrians crossing from the right island.
- **Minute 84** — traffic queues built from ~45s (only stated queue build-up).
- Otherwise no congestion, jams or stoppages in live lanes were observed at any point; traffic was described as steady-to-heavy at peak but free-flowing in every period.

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS

- **Helmetless riders** — repeatedly noted: minutes 9, 14, 54, 156 (two riders, stopped on zebra), 261 (two riders, final frames), 275, 525/600-624 period (some unhelmeted), 709 (many without helmets).
- **Red-signal crossings** — two-wheelers repeatedly observed crossing on red/amber phases (minutes 525, 529, 545); traffic moved freely despite camera-facing red at minutes 702 and 709.
- **Zebra-crossing misuse** — scooter stopped on zebra with two helmetless riders (minute 156); two-wheeler on footpath side of zebra (minute 43); black-and-yellow three-wheeler crossing diagonally over the zebra (minute 160); auto-rickshaw stationary on zebra/stop line (minute 296); SUV/ambulance-type vehicle braking across the zebra (minute 540); pedestrians standing in live carriageway (minutes 12 ~50–55s, 119, 572).
- **Parking/stopping** — white car parked with driver door open at kerb (minute 62); black car parked at left kerb throughout minute 79; auto-rickshaw parked at kerb through minutes 695–698.
- No wrong-way driving was recorded.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY

The junction ran continuously for 12 hours with no gaps, collisions or serious incidents. The footage divides into a long night phase (minutes 0–~524), during which traffic was steady-to-heavy early (minutes 0–150: buses, trucks and pedestrians most frequent, with queuing at minute 84), tapering to light, free-flowing flow through the late night (minutes ~325–524) with infrared/greyscale imagery around minutes 500–519; a dusk/dawn transition (~minutes 519–624) with signal phases showing red/amber to camera and light traffic; and an overcast daylight phase (minutes ~625–719) with the busiest sustained mixed flow of the later half — 10–25 two-wheelers and 4–15 auto-rickshaws per minute. The dominant traffic at every stage was two-wheelers and yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws with white cars; buses of many liveries recurred throughout. Pedestrian activity was heaviest in the first three hours (families, groups, people waiting at kerbs) and became sparse and individual after minute ~325. Recurring features across the whole period: white ambulance-type vans with flashing lights (at least nine sightings), dogs near the kerb, riders in white/light clothing, parked vehicles at the left kerb, and fleet-named buses/coaches (the only legible text in the footage). The single most significant event was the load spill from a white box truck at minute 200.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS

Quiet stretches, with only light free-flowing traffic, sparse or absent pedestrians and nothing notable:
- **Minutes 300–324** (no observations logged / no notable content reported).
- **Minutes 325–349** — consistently light traffic, zebra otherwise unused, nothing unusual.
- **Minutes 350–374** — no pedestrians used the crossing, no congestion, no incidents.
- **Minutes 400–424** — no pedestrians on the crossing, light traffic.
- **Minutes 425–449** — no accidents, no pedestrians crossing the zebra, scarce people.
- **Minutes 450–474** — no incidents at any point, no pedestrians on crossings.
- **Minutes 475–499** — only one minor event (minute 479), pedestrians rare.
- **Minutes 500–524** — light free-flowing traffic, sparse pedestrians.
- **Minutes 550–624** — consistently light traffic, sparse footpath-only pedestrian activity, nothing untoward.
- **Minutes 675–699 and 700–719** — light-to-moderate routine flow with no collisions, stoppages or flagged violations.

**End of summary.** No vehicle make, model or registration plate was confirmed beyond the single Maruti Suzuki Swift at minute 711; all other class-level observations remain unconfirmed owing to night glare, distance and motion blur.
